[0.007342, "o", "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J"]
[0.007651, "o", "A read-only user just wrote to the backend.\r\n"]
[2.084185, "o", "The agent tool used one shared service account. Watch which identity the backend accepts.\r\n"]
[4.161298, "o", "$ python3 demo.py\r\n"]
[5.260236, "o", "=== §19 case: read-only user + write-capable shared tool cred ===\r\n\r\n1. End user: alice role=reader\r\n2. Tool credential backend will accept: svc-agent-tools can_write=True\r\n\r\n3. BEFORE authZ check: write SUCCEEDED -> T-101\r\n   Credential the backend accepted: svc-agent-tools (not alice)\r\n   Why allowed: backend only saw the shared write-capable tool identity.\r\n\r\n4. Added missing check: tool requires user.role == admin before calling backend\r\n\r\n"]
[5.260263, "o", "5. AFTER authZ check: write FAILED -> authZ check: user alice is reader, write denied\r\n   Same user, same tool, same shared cred. The check changed the outcome.\r\n\r\nTakeaway: follow one action to the identity the backend accepted.\r\nReporting 'user is read-only' without that trace is false assurance.\r\n"]
[8.320992, "o", "\r\nOne check on the users own permission changed the outcome.\r\n"]
[10.342293, "o", "Two adjacent failure modes, same root cause:\r\n"]
[12.35617, "o", "$ python3 kill_switch.py\r\n"]
[13.430274, "o", "=== Kill switch: shared credential vs per-agent identity ===\r\n\r\nSetup: three agents call the same ticket backend.\r\n       support-agent, billing-agent, research-agent (compromised)\r\nQuestion: can we stop the compromised agent without taking down the fleet?\r\n\r\n--- Mode A: all agents share svc-agent-tools ---\r\n\r\n1. Before the kill switch\r\n   Shared credential: svc-agent-tools can_write=True\r\n"]
[13.430347, "o", "   support-agent    write SUCCEEDED -> T-101   cred=svc-agent-tools\r\n   billing-agent    write SUCCEEDED -> T-102   cred=svc-agent-tools\r\n   research-agent   write SUCCEEDED -> T-103   cred=svc-agent-tools\r\n\r\n2. Option A1: do not revoke\r\n   research-agent is still presenting svc-agent-tools\r\n   support-agent    write SUCCEEDED -> T-104   cred=svc-agent-tools\r\n   billing-agent    write SUCCEEDED -> T-105   cred=svc-agent-tools\r\n   research-agent   write SUCCEEDED -> T-106   cred=svc-agent-tools\r\n   Result: the kill switch was not pulled. The compromised agent still writes.\r\n\r\n3. Option A2: revoke the shared credential (collateral damage)\r\n   REVOKED: svc-agent-tools can_write=False\r\n   support-agent    write DENIED    -> backend rejected svc-agent-tools: write not permitted\r\n   billing-agent    write DENIED    -> backend rejected svc-agent-tools: write not permitted\r\n   research-agent   write DENIED    -> backend rejected svc-agent-tools: write not permitted\r\n   Result: the compromised agent stops, and so does"]
[13.430398, "o", " the rest of the fleet.\r\n\r\n--- Mode B: each agent has its own credential ---\r\n\r\n1. Before the kill switch\r\n   support-agent: cred-support-agent can_write=True\r\n   billing-agent: cred-billing-agent can_write=True\r\n   research-agent: cred-research-agent can_write=True\r\n   support-agent    write SUCCEEDED -> T-101   cred=cred-support-agent\r\n   billing-agent    write SUCCEEDED -> T-102   cred=cred-billing-agent\r\n   research-agent   write SUCCEEDED -> T-103   cred=cred-research-agent\r\n\r\n2. Revoke only research-agent\r\n   REVOKED: cred-research-agent can_write=False\r\n   support-agent    write SUCCEEDED -> T-104   cred=cred-support-agent\r\n   billing-agent    write SUCCEEDED -> T-105   cred=cred-billing-agent\r\n   research-agent   write DENIED    -> backend rejected cred-research-agent: write not permitted\r\n   Result: only the compromised agent is stopped. The others keep working.\r\n\r\nTakeaway:\r\n  On a shared service account, the kill switch either takes down the\r\n  fleet or does nothing. A kill switch only works if eac"]
[13.430444, "o", "h agent has\r\n  its own credential.\r\n"]
[16.452898, "o", "$ python3 revoke_after_queue.py\r\n"]
[17.515051, "o", "=== Revoke-after-queue experiment ===\r\n\r\nSetup: alice is admin at enqueue, revoked to reader before execute.\r\nQuestion: is the role checked only at enqueue, or again at execute?\r\n\r\nNote: original demo.py authZ lives in the AgentTool wrapper, not in TicketBackend.\r\n\r\n=== Variant a: no user check (shared credential only) ===\r\n\r\n1. Alice role=admin (can write)\r\n   enqueue: user=alice role_at_enqueue=admin title='delete all invoices'\r\n\r\n2. REVOKED: alice role now=reader\r\n"]
[17.515118, "o", "3. Execute queued write\r\n\r\n4. RESULT: write SUCCEEDED -> T-101\r\n   Credential the backend accepted: svc-agent-tools\r\n   Tickets now: ['T-100 open', 'T-101 delete all invoices']\r\n\r\n=== Variant b: role checked only at enqueue ===\r\n\r\n1. Alice role=admin (can write)\r\n   enqueue: user=alice role_at_enqueue=admin title='delete all invoices'\r\n\r\n2. REVOKED: alice role now=reader\r\n3. Execute queued write\r\n\r\n4. RESULT: write SUCCEEDED -> T-101\r\n   Credential the backend accepted: svc-agent-tools\r\n   Tickets now: ['T-100 open', 'T-101 delete all invoices']\r\n\r\n=== Variant c: role checked again at execute (current role state) ===\r\n\r\n1. Alice role=admin (can write)\r\n"]
[17.515129, "o", "   enqueue: user=alice role_at_enqueue=admin title='delete all invoices'\r\n\r\n2. REVOKED: alice role now=reader\r\n3. Execute queued write\r\n\r\n4. RESULT: write FAILED -> authZ at execute: user alice is reader, write denied\r\n   Tickets unchanged: ['T-100 open']\r\n\r\nTakeaway:\r\n  (a) revoke is invisible — shared cred still writes.\r\n  (b) stale enqueue allow rides through after revoke.\r\n  (c) re-check at execute denies the revoked write.\r\nCheck role when the write executes, not only when it is queued.\r\n"]
[20.562411, "o", "\r\nTakeaway: trace each action to the identity the backend actually accepted.\r\n"]
